  "description": "If you love ceviche, then Mexico's aguachile is for you. Traditionally made with raw shrimp, lime juice, chilies, cucumber, and onion, it's served immediately while still totally raw, unlike most other ceviche recipes. This recipe is about as close to the classic as you can get, and it's delicious.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 1 hr 5 min to 2 hr 5 min.\n\nOptional or for serving: Tostadas and sliced avocado, for serving\n\nOptional substitutions: sashimi-grade head-on shrimp → 12 medium shrimp; Sea salt → kosher salt",
